From: ahmedawachi <121810925+ahmedawachi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:35:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] deps: build xxhash with an optimization level

What: deps/Makefile now passes an explicit level to xxhash: the
OPTIMIZATION given on the make command line (for example -O2, or -O0 for a
fallback build), else -O2. A level in CFLAGS still wins because it comes
last. Resulting xxhash CFLAGS:
  make                                      -> -fPIC -O2
  make OPTIMIZATION=-O2 CFLAGS=-Wno-char-subscripts
                                            -> -fPIC -O2 -Wno-char-subscripts
  make OPTIMIZATION=-O0                     -> -fPIC -O0
  make CFLAGS=-O0                           -> -fPIC -O2 -O0 (-O0 wins)

Why: xxhash's own Makefile sets
"CFLAGS ?= -O3", but deps/Makefile always passes CFLAGS on the command
line, which overrides it. So libxxhash.a builds at the compiler default
-O0 in every upstream build, including an
OPTIMIZATION=-O2 build (its build log shows
"cc -fPIC -Wno-char-subscripts ... -c xxhash.c"). OPTIMIZATION alone
does not reach xxhash, unlike hiredis (its own OPTIMIZATION variable),
lua (-O2 in deps/Makefile), and linenoise/hdr_histogram/fpconv/tre (-Os
in their own Makefiles). Still needed after the switch to -O2.

Risk: very low. The impact is also low: XXH3 is used by the string
digest paths (t_string.c) and streams. Build-flag-only change on every
platform.
---
 deps/Makefile | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/deps/Makefile b/deps/Makefile
index 7ca6de4..e098d4a 100644
--- a/deps/Makefile
+++ b/deps/Makefile
@@ -102,7 +102,12 @@ tre: .make-prerequisites
 .PHONY: tre
 
 
-XXHASH_CFLAGS = -fPIC $(DEPS_CFLAGS)
+# xxhash's Makefile sets -O3 with "CFLAGS ?=", which the CFLAGS passed below
+# overrides, so without a level here it builds at the compiler default -O0.
+# Follow an OPTIMIZATION given on the make command line, else use -O2. A level
+# in CFLAGS still wins because DEPS_CFLAGS comes last.
+XXHASH_OPT := $(if $(OPTIMIZATION),$(OPTIMIZATION),-O2)
+XXHASH_CFLAGS = -fPIC $(XXHASH_OPT) $(DEPS_CFLAGS)
 xxhash: .make-prerequisites
 	@printf '%b %b\n' $(MAKECOLOR)MAKE$(ENDCOLOR) $(BINCOLOR)$@$(ENDCOLOR)
 	cd xxhash && $(MAKE) lib CFLAGS="$(XXHASH_CFLAGS)" LDFLAGS="$(DEPS_LDFLAGS)"
